gsipper (1.0.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Status-menu Connect / Reconnect now also flip 'Account > Enabled'
    back on if it had been toggled off there. Previously, if the
    user disabled the account in Account settings, the status dot
    menu's Connect would call set_registration(True), the worker
    fell back to configure_account(load_settings().account), and
    that saw enabled=False -> 'Not configured', staying offline.
    Now the window saves the settings change before submitting,
    so the worker's load_settings() picks up enabled=True and a
    fresh REGISTER actually fires. The Account dialog also reports
    Enabled = on next time the user opens it, matching their
    intent of being online from now on.

